A||||4||drednot||could/should I remove my cat. converter?||||6||
Z||000000||drednot||04-12-2001||09:22 PM||||what benefits would I get from removing my stock catalytic converter?  I was considering taking it off after my next inspection, and the re-installing it before my next inspection.  what do you think?  I know that the exhaust system will be less restrictive once I take the cat off, but will that transfer to it sounding better and gaining performance?  What do you think? ||||reg||6
Z||000001||88formula||04-12-2001||09:31 PM||||The sound will get loader and throaty. You will loose a few foot-lbs. of torque and gain something like 2 horsepower at the upper end of the rpm band. There is a guy here named 1FST2M6 that had his car put on a dynamometer before and after the converter was removed. In my opinion it's definitely not worth the trouble of removing the cat and putting it back on again for inspection. It’s not worth the effort. I'm sure he would tell you the same.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||drednot||04-12-2001||09:33 PM||||The sound will get loader and throaty you say??  OK!!  I want it!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||04-12-2001||09:53 PM||||I did it when I had the stock V6 in my 86GT.  The sound was perfect!!!  What I did was buy an after market, high flow cat.  I put flanges on it so it could easily be removed.  Then I had a straight pipe with flanges made up the exact length of the cat.  This allowed me to remove and install the cat at will, without having to go to a muffler shop.  It's easy and like I said the sound is great!<P>Jay<BR>1986 GT Northstar <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||04-12-2001||09:58 PM||||replace it with a 22" straight cherry bomb muffler with 2 1/4" outlets that will fit over the stock pipe. You probably won't notice a horsepower gain, but the sound is hugely worth the effort. Cherry bomb costs less than $20 and they are everywhere. I did this first with just a straight pipe, but it was way loud and not a good loud. Sounded kinda tinny.<P>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 04-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
